  "worked_solution": "A quadrilateral has $n=4$ sides, so the sum of its interior angles must be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom step 5, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & =m∠FAO={45}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠O & =m∠AOE={140}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196588/assets/f67441e3999a8b81e7ac63555c729f0f6c31bff015477efc3031364c6fb22003.png)\n\nAdding up the interior angles, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠O+m∠E+m∠F & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {45}^{∘}+{140}^{∘}+{65}^{∘}+m∠F & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {250}^{∘}+m∠F & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ m∠F & ={110}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $m∠F={110}^{∘}.$",
